<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Jersey</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">New Jersey is a state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> between the Hudson and Delaware rivers. Taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> in 1664, it was granted to Lord Berkeley and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-carteret">Sir George Carteret</a> and divided into East and West Jersey before being reunited as a royal province in 1702. In 1776 it adopted a state constitution and joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolution">American Revolution</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/new-jersey.jpg" alt="New Jersey" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: author of xrmap, with modifications by Denelson83 and ChrisRuvolo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_New_Jersey.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
